\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Naturalness landscape for the four minimal-ECH dark-energy routes} (R1 NJL, R2 one-loop effective action, R3 Immirzi running, R4 parity-CMB spectator-ALP). Each route is shown as a point in the (mass$\!\times \!$coupling) plane required to source $\rho _\Lambda $ at the observed value, with the naturalness window (gray band) defined by the scale of the underlying physics ($M_{\rm  Pl}$ for R3, $H_0$ for R4 spectator-ALP via the cosmological-constant-class tuning admitted in \S  \ref {sec:r4_birefringence}). All four routes either sit outside the naturalness window or require a $m_\theta \!\sim \!H_0$ tuning that re-imports the cosmological-constant problem. The 13 logically-independent barriers (Table~\ref {tab:barriers}) constrain the routes at the amplitude level.}}{14}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:naturalness}{{5}{14}{\textbf {Naturalness landscape for the four minimal-ECH dark-energy routes} (R1 NJL, R2 one-loop effective action, R3 Immirzi running, R4 parity-CMB spectator-ALP). Each route is shown as a point in the (mass$\!\times \!$coupling) plane required to source $\rho _\Lambda $ at the observed value, with the naturalness window (gray band) defined by the scale of the underlying physics ($M_{\rm Pl}$ for R3, $H_0$ for R4 spectator-ALP via the cosmological-constant-class tuning admitted in \S \ref {sec:r4_birefringence}). All four routes either sit outside the naturalness window or require a $m_\theta \!\sim \!H_0$ tuning that re-imports the cosmological-constant problem. The 13 logically-independent barriers (Table~\ref {tab:barriers}) constrain the routes at the amplitude level}{figure.5}{}}
